# {{project-name}}

A [Murphy](https://github.com/murphy-rs/murphy) plugin pack — generated from
[`murphy-rs/plugin-template`](https://github.com/murphy-rs/plugin-template).

Ships one demo cop, `Example/NoTodo` (flags bare `todo(...)` placeholders).
It exists only as a build-and-load smoke target: **delete it when starting
a real pack** (remove `src/lib.rs`'s `NoTodo`, the `provided` entry in
`murphy-plugin.toml`, and `tests/smoke.rs`'s demo assertions), then add real
cops following Murphy's
[plugin-cop-infrastructure guide](https://github.com/murphy-rs/murphy/blob/main/docs/guides/plugin-cop-infrastructure.md).

## Prerequisites

- Rust (stable) — the pack builds as a `cdylib`.
- [`cargo-generate`](https://cargo-generate.github.io/cargo-generate/) — only
  needed once, to scaffold (this pack is already scaffolded).
- A Murphy checkout or release whose `MURPHY_PLUGIN_ABI_VERSION` matches
  `murphy-api-version` in `murphy-plugin.toml` (currently `4`).

> Until `murphy-plugin-api` is published to crates.io, point `Cargo.toml`'s
> `murphy-plugin-api` entries at a git/path dependency on the Murphy repo's
> `crates/murphy-plugin-api` (see the comment in `Cargo.toml`).

## Build and test

```sh
cargo test
cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo fmt --check
```

`cargo test` runs `tests/smoke.rs`: the demo cop fires on bare `todo` through
the public `test_support` harness, and the pack-registration test asserts
`PACK_COPS` matches `[cops].provided` in `murphy-plugin.toml`.

## Load it in Murphy

Build the shared library, then stage it as a pack directory (ADR 0046):

```sh
cargo build
PACK={{project-name}}
mkdir -p /tmp/murphy-packs/$PACK/lib/linux-x86_64
cp -f target/debug/lib{{crate_name}}.so /tmp/murphy-packs/$PACK/lib/linux-x86_64/
cp -f murphy-plugin.toml /tmp/murphy-packs/$PACK/
```

Point Murphy at the pack directory from `.murphy.yml`:

```yaml
plugins:
  - name: {{project-name}}
    path: /tmp/murphy-packs/{{project-name}}
```

then lint a fixture containing a bare `todo`:

```sh
printf 'todo("finish me")\n' > /tmp/todo_sample.rb
murphy lint --format json /tmp/todo_sample.rb
```

Expect one `Example/NoTodo` offense. (A direct `.so` path also works for
quick iteration; the pack directory is the distributable form.)

## Writing real cops

- Authoring surface (`#[cop]`, `#[on_node]`, options, testing): Murphy's
  `docs/guides/plugin-cop-infrastructure.md`.
- Pack format (manifest schema, `lib/<arch>/` layout, search-path rules):
  ADR 0046 in the Murphy repo (`docs/decisions/0046-plugin-pack-format.md`).
- Single-surface rule: runtime `[dependencies]` must stay exactly
  `{murphy-plugin-api}` — reaching into `murphy-core` / `murphy-ast` etc.
  breaks the plugin ABI boundary.

